    "note": "PRIORITY RAISED 11 -> 40, 2026-08-11. Same correction as z08 and for the same reason — the relict beach-ridge belt was losing to the mesic-prairie elevation band that runs across it. 40 sits just below the lakeshore at 45 so that where the two boxes meet at E +1400 the open beach wins over the older ridges, which is the seaward order. PLANTABLE SINCE 2026-08-11. This community was written and then withheld: the ground it describes did not exist in the model. ROADMAP S2e has since extended the heightfield east from a 640 m square to E -320..+1700, and this zone's extent now matches 14,577 samples of the committed terrain, so it is planted. Nothing about the species, the July phenology or the confidence has changed — the records were always ready and the ground was not. WHAT THE ORIGINAL NOTE SAID, kept because it was correct when it was written: PLANTABLE SINCE 2026-08-11, when ROADMAP S2e parcel (b) carried the heightfield east to E +1700. The relict beach-ridge belt runs from the State Street break-of-slope — the terrain spec builds that band between E +780 and +880, centred on the two State Street ground-control points at E +837.6 and +822.5 — east to the lakeshore sand ridges, and all of it is modelled ground now, standing at +7.6 to +9.5 ft above the water. The north-south bounds are the scene's own, not the belt's. NOT FIXED HERE, for the flora parcel: at priority 11 this zone loses everywhere to z02_mesic_prairie (priority 22), so the dry sand prairie is currently planted as mesic prairie — the opposite of the 10-25 per cent bare sand this record exists to state."
  },
